{{- /*
  support/bootstrap-gate — first-run playbook setup for a Slack support
  channel. Owner: `Support: watch channel`.

  Runs BEFORE the per-iteration channel scope gate. Its job is to make
  sure the three MANDATORY fragments (`scope.md`, `investigation.md`,
  `escalation.md`) exist for the channel before any triage/reply work
  begins, so lazily-owned prompts (`Support: investigate`, `Support: reply
  to user`) never block a silent scheduled run on a UI form nobody sees.

  Idempotent: reads each fragment's presence via FileExists at render
  time. When all three mandatory fragments are already present, the gate
  short-circuits with a one-line "already bootstrapped" note and does
  nothing else.

  Optional fragments (`tone.md`, `resources.md`) are handled by a single
  opt-in `mitto_ui_options` prompt after the mandatory pass — the user
  can decline and add them later via their normal lazy owner-ask paths
  (`Support: reply to user`, `Support: investigate`).

  `redirects.md` is intentionally not offered here: its owner
  (`Support: investigate`) only asks for it on demand the first time an
  out-of-scope question actually arrives, so proactively bootstrapping it
  would waste the user's time.

  Callers pass named fields via a `dict`:

    Channel:  the Slack channel id (e.g. C0XXXXXXX). Required. If empty
              (per-bead callers that do not know the channel at render
              time) the gate emits a short "cannot bootstrap without a
              channel id" note and does nothing — the individual owner
              prompts will still ask lazily.
    Silent:   bool. True for a silent scheduled loop run (nobody is
              watching), false for an interactive / force-triggered run.
              Silent runs use short (60s) timeouts on all forms and, on
              timeout, fall back to a `mitto_ui_notify` warning +
              skip-drafting policy consistent with the existing channel
              scope gate.

  Whitespace: fragment body starts flush at column 1 and emits no
  trailing newline; the caller frames it with its own heading.
*/ -}}
{{- $channel := .Channel -}}
{{- $silent  := .Silent  -}}
{{- $scopePath        := printf ".mitto/support/%s/scope.md"         $channel -}}
{{- $investigatePath  := printf ".mitto/support/%s/investigation.md" $channel -}}
{{- $escalationPath   := printf ".mitto/support/%s/escalation.md"    $channel -}}
{{- $tonePath         := printf ".mitto/support/%s/tone.md"          $channel -}}
{{- $resourcesPath    := printf ".mitto/support/%s/resources.md"     $channel -}}
{{- $scopeOK        := and $channel (FileExists $scopePath) -}}
{{- $investigateOK  := and $channel (FileExists $investigatePath) -}}
{{- $escalationOK   := and $channel (FileExists $escalationPath) -}}
{{- $toneOK         := and $channel (FileExists $tonePath) -}}
{{- $resourcesOK    := and $channel (FileExists $resourcesPath) -}}
{{- $mandatoryAllOK := and $scopeOK $investigateOK $escalationOK -}}
{{- $timeout := 300 -}}{{- if $silent }}{{ $timeout = 60 }}{{ end -}}
{{- if not $channel -}}
**Bootstrap gate — skipped.** No channel id supplied at render time, so
per-channel playbook paths cannot be resolved. Individual owner prompts
(`Support: watch channel`, `Support: investigate`, `Support: reply to
user`) will still ask for their fragments lazily the first time each is
needed.
{{- else if $mandatoryAllOK -}}
**Bootstrap gate — already bootstrapped.** All mandatory playbook
fragments for channel `{{ $channel }}` are present on disk:
- `{{ $scopePath }}` ✓
- `{{ $investigatePath }}` ✓
- `{{ $escalationPath }}` ✓

Optional fragments (informational — the gate does **not** ask for these
here; each is owned by its own prompt and will be requested lazily when
first needed):
- `{{ $tonePath }}` — {{ if $toneOK }}present ✓{{ else }}absent (owned by **Support: reply to user**){{ end }}
- `{{ $resourcesPath }}` — {{ if $resourcesOK }}present ✓{{ else }}absent (owned by **Support: investigate**){{ end }}
- `.mitto/support/{{ $channel }}/redirects.md` — requested on demand by **Support: investigate** the first time an out-of-scope question arrives; do not proactively create.

Skipping bootstrap this iteration. Proceed directly to the channel scope
gate below (it re-checks `scope.md` as a safety net in case the file was
deleted between iterations).
{{- else -}}
**Bootstrap gate — first-run playbook setup for channel `{{ $channel }}`.**
{{- if $silent }} *Silent scheduled run (nobody is watching).* All forms below use a
short `timeout_seconds: {{ $timeout }}`; on timeout, send a `mitto_ui_notify`
warning that the channel has not been bootstrapped yet, then continue triage +
reconcile but **skip drafting** this run — the next iteration re-runs this gate.
{{- else }} *Interactive run — a user is present.* This is a one-time, idempotent
setup pass; subsequent iterations short-circuit once all three mandatory
fragments exist on disk.
{{- end }}

Create the `.mitto/support/{{ $channel }}/` directory if it does not exist
(single `mkdir -p`), then work through the two phases below in order.

### Phase 1 — Mandatory fragments (must exist before triage can produce drafts)

Each of the three fragments below is REQUIRED. Skip the ones already present
(marked ✓); ask for the missing ones (marked ✗) using the linked owner-ask
step. Do **not** batch — ask one at a time, write the file after each form
returns, then move on. If any form times out or is aborted, do **not** write
a partial file; log a `[CONTEXT]` note (or `mitto_ui_notify` on a silent run)
and skip that fragment — the gate re-asks it next iteration.

1. **`scope.md`** — what this channel is (and is not) responsible for.
   {{ if $scopeOK }}Already present ✓ — skip.{{ else }}Missing ✗ — ask + write now.
   {{ template "support/shared/ask-scope" (dict "TimeoutSeconds" $timeout) }}
   {{ end }}
2. **`investigation.md`** — how to investigate questions on this channel
   (tool order, safe commands, MCP/CLI tools, confidence rules).
   {{ if $investigateOK }}Already present ✓ — skip.{{ else }}Missing ✗ — ask + write now.
   {{ template "support/shared/ask-investigation" (dict "TimeoutSeconds" $timeout) }}
   {{ end }}
3. **`escalation.md`** — who / when / how to escalate for this channel.
   {{ if $escalationOK }}Already present ✓ — skip.{{ else }}Missing ✗ — ask + write now.
   {{ template "support/shared/ask-escalation" (dict "TimeoutSeconds" $timeout) }}
   {{ end }}

### Phase 2 — Optional fragments (skip by default; opt in on demand)

{{ if $silent -}}
On a silent scheduled run, **do not** ask about optional fragments — send a
single `mitto_ui_notify` (info style) noting which optional fragments are
absent and that they will be requested by their owner prompts (`Support:
reply to user`, `Support: investigate`) the next time an interactive run
needs them. Then proceed to the channel scope gate below.
{{- else -}}
After Phase 1 completes, ask the user **once** whether to bootstrap any
optional fragments now. Skip this ask entirely if BOTH `tone.md` and
`resources.md` are already present (marked ✓ below).

- `{{ $tonePath }}` — {{ if $toneOK }}present ✓{{ else }}absent (owned by **Support: reply to user**){{ end }}
- `{{ $resourcesPath }}` — {{ if $resourcesOK }}present ✓{{ else }}absent (owned by **Support: investigate**){{ end }}

{{ if not (and $toneOK $resourcesOK) -}}
Open `mitto_ui_options` (`timeout_seconds: {{ $timeout }}`) titled
"Add optional playbook fragments now?" with a short description explaining
that these are optional (the owner prompts will ask for them lazily if
skipped now) and these choices:
- **Skip both** — the default. Send a `mitto_ui_notify` (info) reminding
  the user that `tone.md` / `resources.md` can be added later by running
  **Support: reply to user** / **Support: investigate** on any bead in
  this channel (their owner-ask steps will fire the first time each is
  missing).
{{ if not $toneOK -}}
- **Add `tone.md` only** — invoke the reply-to-user owner-ask below.
{{ end -}}
{{ if not $resourcesOK -}}
- **Add `resources.md` only** — invoke the investigate owner-ask below.
{{ end -}}
{{ if and (not $toneOK) (not $resourcesOK) -}}
- **Add both** — invoke both owner-asks below, one after the other.
{{ end }}

{{ if not $toneOK -}}
**Optional owner-ask — `tone.md`** (only run if the user opted in above):
{{ template "support/shared/ask-tone" (dict "TimeoutSeconds" $timeout) }}
{{ end -}}
{{ if not $resourcesOK -}}
**Optional owner-ask — `resources.md`** (only run if the user opted in above):
{{ template "support/shared/ask-resources" (dict "TimeoutSeconds" $timeout) }}
{{ end -}}
{{ else -}}
Both optional fragments are already present — nothing to ask.
{{ end -}}

**`redirects.md`** is intentionally **not** offered here. Its owner
(`Support: investigate`) requests it on demand the first time an
out-of-scope question actually arrives on this channel, so proactively
creating it would waste the user's time.
{{- end }}

After Phase 2 completes (or is skipped), proceed to the channel scope
gate below. The scope gate re-checks `scope.md` as a safety net in case
the file was deleted between iterations, and reads `tone.md` if it is
present.
{{- end -}}
{{- /* no trailing newline */ -}}
